:: Carter Hero's Weakness Part 3 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 10>>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright, we’re inside.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says as the two of you sneak through the kitchen and dinning room of his house. <span style="color:LightGreen">He had turned out the lights to give the entire house a dark and mysterious vibe that fits that of an evil lair.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“From our intel, we know that the villain has stolen a device from Galaxy Labs that can be used to mind control other heroes! We can’t let such a thing sit in the hands of an evil-doer, so we have to recover it. It has been stashed in my brother’s room, so you head there, I’m going to look around the living room to try and see if I can’t find more details on their plan. I’ll meet you over there!”</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                },
                },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

You give <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> a heroic salute and begin to crouch towards the hallway, keeping low to avoid detection from any remaining guard. You could probably take them in a fight, but don’t want to risk alerting the main villain to your presence. The dark hallway looms ahead of you, seeming to stretch out in the pitch black into some kind of endless walkway of evilness. You look towards the door next to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>’s room. <span style="color:Yellow">It would make sense that it would be there, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s own alternate universe double’s own chambers. It fits, so probably why <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> didn’t seem to mention which brother’s room.</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">It’s all too perfect.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:Yellow">It also helps that you’re curious about his room, not having seen inside of it yet due to his brother’s more solitary nature.</span> You try to picture what could be inside as you slowly creep over and turn the doorknob. Unlocked and empty, you believe. The room’s light is off and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> had said he’d be home alone. <span style="color:Yellow">You really hope so, since walking in on his brother would be a very awkward first interaction.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Open the door">>
    <span style="color:Yellow">The air seems to grow colder as you open the door, the room’s temperature much chillier than the rest of the house.</span> Your eyes take a second to adjust to the near total darkness of the room, the blinds pulled shut. The room is spotless and neat, a large contrast to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s. You spy some posters on the wall for various movies and video games, all with the same edgy, dark vibe associated with preteens wanting to be cool. <span style="color:Pink">Though you do notice a few that stand out, a poster about a team-up between Ultraman and Owlman along with a rather cute small poster of a children’s cartoon you’ve seen your brother watch before. They make for a cute contrast between the rest of the room.</span> <br>
    <br>
    The desk has a small shelf full of a few books, games, and comics. They are all neatly organized and some are coated in dust, not having been touched in a while, though a decent few have fingerprints on them from being held recently. The most surprising part of the room sits on the bed, next to a still warm pile of recently washed clothes. <span style="color:Pink">A stuffed Owlman bear, much like <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s Ultraman one. It looks much better taken care of than <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s, though this may be due to it not being used as a villain in his make-believe games. They must have come in a set, one for each brother. It’s kind of adorable actually.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                },
                },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    Blush: 2,
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What are you doing in here!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> calls out, <span style="color:LightCoral">quickly grabbing you by the hand and yanking you a bit harshly towards the door.</span> You yelp a bit in surprise, pulling your hand away and rubbing it. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, I didn’t mean to pull that hard. But we- I don’t want us in here. Please…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> <span style="color:LightCoral">looks towards the door, his face quickly becoming downtrodden. You feel a pain in your chest and nod, allowing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to lead you back into the hallway and close the door.</span> Warmth seems to return to the hallway as soon as he does. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I meant <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>’s room, not…”</span> He grumbles to himself, <span style="color:Yellow">looking at the ground with an upset expression,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, it’s not your fault. I should have been more clear…”</span> You apologize, saying you didn’t mean to make him upset and thought he meant this room since it made sense. With the evil doppelganger and- <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He’s not my evil doppelganger!”</span> <span style="color:LightCoral">He snaps at you a little harshly, causing you to take a step back,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He’s just”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> sighs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, I don’t want to be mad at you. I shouldn’t be, but… I just thought being home alone meant I could get away with a day that didn’t involve… him.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> stares at the ground, <span style="color:LightCoral">feeling as though his outburst may have ruined the mood.</span> You sit in silence for a moment, trying to think of a way to help. <br>
    <br>

    <div id="choice">
        <<link "Comfort him<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            <span style="color:Pink">You walk over and give <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> a hug to try and comfort him, apologizing again.</span> You want to ask him about why he’s so upset about his brother, but get the feeling that asking will only make it worse, so you drop the topic for now and remind him that you came over to hang out with him, no one else. This day is just about the two of you having fun and being heroes. With that in mind, shouldn’t you two be working to stop this evil villain before it’s too late? <br>
            <br>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah, we should.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> smiles, the pink in his cheeks fading, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Let’s go! Before he realizes we’re here!”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">With that, the two of you head off towards <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>’s room, determined to put an end to this devious plot!</span> <br>
            <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|Carter Hero's Weakness Part 4]]<br>
        <</replace>>
        <</link>>
        <<link "Lighten the mood<br>">>
        <<replace "#choice">>
            In order to lighten the mood and break the tension in the air, you quickly grab <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> and yank him down to the floor. He looks at you in confusion before you say that some guards are coming this way and you have to be quiet. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> <span style="color:Pink">sees what you are doing and smiles, nodding and you both move behind a nearby shelf and crouch behind it.</span> Once the guards are gone, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> turns to you in a hushed tone. <br>
            <br>
            <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We should get moving. We have to get the mind control device before he realizes we are here, come on!”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">With that, the two of you head off towards <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>’s room, determined to put an end to this devious plot!</span> <br>
            <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
            <br>
            [[Continue|Carter Hero's Weakness Part 4]]<br>
        <</replace>>
        <</link>>
    </div>
<</linkreplace>>